WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.045
You want to learn Kubernetes.

2
00:00:02.065 --> 00:00:05.205
But a cloud cluster costs money every hour.

3
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:06.618
And you already know Docker.

4
00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:08.115
So start there.

5
00:00:08.135 --> 00:00:13.490
This port gives you three things: the tools, a cluster, and an image to sail with.

6
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.825
First: where does the cluster run?

7
00:00:15.845 --> 00:00:21.110
A tool named kind runs every Kubernetes node as one Docker container.

8
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.045
You start three nodes: one control plane and two workers.

9
00:00:25.065 --> 00:00:29.920
It is free, it starts in a minute, and you can delete it at any time.

10
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.055
Second: you need two tools.

11
00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:33.580
kind builds the cluster.

12
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.390
You use it a few times.

13
00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.490
The second tool talks to the cluster.

14
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:40.540
You use it all day, on any cluster.

15
00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:43.400
Third: the image you take through every port.

16
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.100
Tugboat is a small web app.

17
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.185
You deploy it, scale it, break it and secure it.

18
00:00:48.205 --> 00:00:51.047
A kind node cannot see the images on your laptop.

19
00:00:51.067 --> 00:00:53.985
So you load the image into the nodes.

20
00:00:54.005 --> 00:00:55.970
Quick recap of the setup.

21
00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.432
A node is a container.

22
00:00:57.452 --> 00:00:59.445
One tool builds, one tool talks.

23
00:00:59.465 --> 00:01:01.055
And load your image.

24
00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:04.175
Now start the first lesson below.
